/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:74:Attach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:75:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:76:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:77:- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:78:- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:79:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:80:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:81:- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:82:- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:83:- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. 
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:84:- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:85:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:86:Key insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:87:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:88:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:89:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:90:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="train" puzzle_id="494ef9d7" lines="16-30">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:91:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:92:Slide each blue/teal or yellow/orange row pair together while preserving its left-to-right order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:93:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:94:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:95:- The grid has a black background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:96:- Each nonempty row contains exactly two distinct foreground pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:97:- Blue/teal and yellow/orange row pairs are the moving pairs; other color pairs are distractors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:98:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:99:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:100:- For each moving pair, keep the left pixel fixed and move the right pixel left until it touches the left pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:101:- Clear the moved pixel's original location, and leave non-moving rows unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:102:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:103:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:104:- Only same-hue-family pixel pairs attract horizontally; separated unrelated colors do not compact.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:105:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:106:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:107:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:108:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="train" puzzle_id="1b8318e3" lines="86-105">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:109:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:110:Move each isolated colored pixel into the one-cell frame around a grey 2x2 block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:111:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:112:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:113:- Background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:114:- Grey foreground objects are solid 2x2 anchor blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:115:- Every other non-background, non-grey cell is a colored singleton source.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:116:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:117:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:118:- Keep the grey anchors fixed and clear all colored singleton source pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:119:- For each singleton and each anchor, the normal destination is the cell reached by
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:120:  clamping the pixel into the anchor's one-cell outer frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:121:- If a diagonally outside singleton has an exact 8-direction sightline into an anchor,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:122:  also allow the cell just before the first grey pixel on that ray.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:123:- Choose distinct destinations that minimize total king-move distance; at equal
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:124:  distance prefer exact sightlines, then the shorter Manhattan movement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:125:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:126:Key insight: The grey 2x2 blocks define magnetic frames; conflicts are resolved
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:127:structurally by nearest-frame assignment rather than by color identity.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:128:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:129:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:130:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:131:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="eval" puzzle_id="cb2d8a2c" lines="13-26">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:132:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:133:Extend a green path from one grid edge to the opposite, routing around red bars at a distance dictated by their blue pixel count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:134:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:135:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:136:- bg = azure (8). Red/blue bars (color 2/1) act as obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:137:- A single green (3) pixel sits on a grid border — the path start.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:138:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:139:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:140:- Each bar's keep-out radius equals its number of blue pixels; the path must stay farther than that from every bar cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:141:- The green pixel extends inward toward the opposite edge, turning at right angles to navigate around forbidden zones.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:142:- After the path is drawn, all blue pixels become red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:143:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:144:Key insight: Blue pixels on a bar encode its danger radius — more blue means a wider no-go zone the path must respect.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:145:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:146:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:147:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:148:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="train" puzzle_id="bae5c565" lines="10-28">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:149:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:150:Erase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:151:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:152:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:153:- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:154:- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:155:- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:156:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:157:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:158:- Clear the grid to background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:159:- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:160:  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:161:- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:162:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:163:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:164:- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:165:  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:166:  the expansion begins.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:167:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:168:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:170:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="train" puzzle_id="2f767503" lines="66-81">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:171:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:172:Erase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:173:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:174:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:175:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:176:- There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:177:- The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:178:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:179:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:180:- Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:181:- Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:182:- Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:183:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:184:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:185:- The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:186:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:187:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:188:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:189:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="train" puzzle_id="f341894c" lines="63-78">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:190:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:191:Reorient each two-pixel blue/pink segment so it reads pink then blue when viewed from its border marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:192:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:193:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:194:- The background is dominant, with one border-only marker color and blue/pink foreground segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:195:- Every marker lies on the outer border and points inward along its row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:196:- Along exactly one inward ray from each marker is a single adjacent two-pixel blue/pink segment.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:198:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:199:- For each marker, look inward perpendicular to the border side containing the marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:200:- Rewrite the two blue/pink pixels on that ray so the nearer one is pink and the farther one is blue.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:201:- Keep marker pixels, background pixels, and all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:203:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:204:- The marker gives a local viewing direction; the segment's required order is relative to that marker, not to global row or column order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:205:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:206:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:207:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:208:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="1e5d6875" lines="26-45">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:209:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:210:Paint a recolored diagonal copy from each L triomino source object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:211:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:212:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:213:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:214:- The only foreground objects are 4-connected red and grey L triominoes,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:215:  each occupying three pixels of a 2x2 box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:217:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:218:- Grey L objects paint a yellow copy translated one diagonal step toward
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:219:  their missing 2x2 corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:220:- Red L objects paint a green copy translated one diagonal step away from
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:221:  their missing 2x2 corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:222:- Copies are clipped by the grid boundary; red-derived green copies are
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:223:  painted after grey-derived yellow copies where the projections collide.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:224:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:225:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:226:- The missing corner of each 2x2 L object identifies its diagonal axis, and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:227:  the source color determines which side of that axis receives the copy.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:228:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:229:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:230:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:231:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="6350f1f4" lines="62-81">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:232:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:233:Decode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:235:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:236:The grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:237:square blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:238:uniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:239:cells that act as wildcards.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:241:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:242:Infer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:243:block matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:244:the sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:245:Separator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:246:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:247:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:248:The small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:249:uniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:250:opposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:251:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:252:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:253:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:254:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="b71a7747" lines="10-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:255:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:256:Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:257:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:258:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:259:The grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:260:cross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:261:the surrounding filler or separators.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:262:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:263:Find that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:264:the pair, and return the induced subgrid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:265:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:266:The target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:267:whose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:268:deleting unused rows and columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:269:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:270:</reference_puzzle>
