/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:314:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:315:Crop a board cluster and rotate its color layers based on outside cue sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:316:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:317:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:318:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:319:- A main multi-color board cluster (largest foreground region).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:320:- Small monochrome cue sprites outside the board for the colors that rotate.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:321:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:322:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:323:- Tight-crop around the board cluster.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:324:- For each color layer inside the crop, find its same-color cue outside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:325:- Rotate that layer clockwise by (cue pixel count mod 4) × 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:326:- No outside cue → no rotation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:327:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:328:Key insight: Cue sprite size mod 4 encodes rotation amount for its matching color layer.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:329:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:330:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:331:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:332:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="train" puzzle_id="6cbe9eb8" lines="79-94">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:333:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:334:Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:335:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:336:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:337:- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:338:- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:339:- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:340:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:341:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:342:- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:343:- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:344:- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:345:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:346:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:347:- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:348:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:349:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:350:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:351:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="b9e38dc0" lines="7-18">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:352:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:353:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:354:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:355:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:356:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:357:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:358:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:359:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:360:- Obstacles cast "shadows" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:362:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:363:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:364:</reference_puzzle>
