/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:367:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:368:Swap every sprite to the opposite prototype while preserving scale and position.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:369:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:370:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:371:- bg = most common color. Two distinct small sprite patterns (prototypes) appear at various scales.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:372:- Each sprite instance is a scaled copy of one of the two prototypes, placed on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:373:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:374:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:375:- Identify the two prototype patterns from the smallest-area sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:376:- For each sprite, determine which prototype it matches and its integer scale factor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:377:- Replace it with the other prototype at the same scale, aligned by an internal anchor region (color-1 pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:378:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:379:Key insight: Every sprite toggles to the alternate prototype; the anchor sub-region inside each sprite pins the alignment so swapped sprites land in the correct position regardless of scale.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:380:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1107365848/17/prompt.md:381:</reference_puzzle>
